+/*
+ * freequay: compatibility rules per program
+ *
+ * Open counterpart of CrossOver's closed cxcompatdb.so. The rules come from text files listed
+ * in FREEQUAY_COMPAT_FILES (separated by colons; for every setting the first file that has it
+ * wins). One rule per line:
+ *
+ *     <key> TAB <directive> [TAB <directive> ...]
+ *
+ * Keys:
+ *     steam:<appid>     the game Steam started (SteamAppId or SteamGameId in its environment)
+ *     exe:<name.exe>    a program file name, or exe:\path\tail.exe for the end of its path
+ *
+ * Directives applied when a process starts:
+ *     backend=<name>        graphics backend, DLLs from the directory in FREEQUAY_BACKEND_<name>
+ *     env=<NAME>=<value>    environment variable; an empty value removes it
+ *     dll=<name>=<order>    DLL load order (n, b, n,b, b,n; empty disables the DLL)
+ *     args=<text>           appended to the command line
+ *     argdel=<text>         removed from the command line
+ *     exe=<from>><to>       start <to> instead of the program whose path ends in <from>
+ *
+ * Command line directives from a steam: key only apply to the first program of the game that
+ * runs from steamapps\common, not to installers, crash handlers or programs the game starts.
+ * Other directives (verb=, reg=, winver= ...) are for "freequay fix" and are skipped here.
+ *
